hy they're returning 308 redirects, maybe a misconfiguration in the service's routing rules.\n</think>\n\nexec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nThe `ad` service exists as a ClusterIP but its reachability and pod health need verification. I will check the service's endpoints and pod status using `kubectl get endpoints ad -n astronomy-shop` and `kubectl get pods -l app=ad -n astronomy-shop` to ensure the service is properly routing traffic to healthy pods. This will confirm if the 308 redirects stem from service misconfiguration or pod unavailability.", additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 493, 'prompt_tokens': 11584, 'total_tokens': 12077, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfed2-78b1-7f73-8164-248b56b132ae-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 11584, 'output_tokens': 493, 'total_tokens': 12077}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='fe3468f3-0b7a-44ac-aff5-87aa55037ec1'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is trying to diagnose an issue with the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application. They've already checked the pods and found them all running. Then they looked at metrics and traces, which showed some 308 Permanent Redirects from the frontend to the ad service. The dependency graph shows frontend calling ad, and the operations list includes calls to AdService/GetAds.\n\nThe next step was to check the ad service's Kubernetes service and endpoints. The service exists as a ClusterIP, but they need to ensure that the endpoints are correctly set up and that the pods are healthy. So, the user should run `kubectl get endpoints ad -n astronomy-shop` to check if the