expected behavior causing the 308 Permanent Redirects. This will directly reveal issues within the service's implementation or environment.", additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 468, 'prompt_tokens': 11804, 'total_tokens': 12272, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfed2-a1cb-7411-ad77-34f8919226d8-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 11804, 'output_tokens': 468, 'total_tokens': 12272}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='0deff229-132c-456c-bab9-b75d70b47d53'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is trying to diagnose an issue with the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application. The problem seems to be related to the frontend service causing 308 Permanent Redirects when calling the ad service. \n\nFirst, they checked the pods and found all are running. Then they looked at metrics and traces, which showed some 308 responses. The dependency graph showed frontend calling ad, and the operations listed 'oteldemo.AdService/GetAds' as a client operation. \n\nNext, they checked the service and endpoints for 'ad', which were present. Now, they need to check the logs of the ad pod to see what's causing the redirects. The last step was to get the endpoints, which were correct. So the next logical step is to look into the pod logs to find out why the ad service is returning 308. \n\nThe user should use `kubectl logs` on the specific ad pod. The command would be `kubectl logs ad-6c7d4665cc-h454d -n astronomy-shop`. This will show the logs for that pod, which might indicate misconfigurations, routing issues, or other problems causing the redirects. Once they have t