e problem seems to be related to the frontend service causing 308 Permanent Redirects when calling the ad service. \n\nFirst, they checked the pods and services, confirming that the ad service exists and has endpoints. But when they tried to get the logs of a specific pod (ad-6c7d4665cc-h454d), it wasn\'t found. That means the pod name might have changed or the pod isn\'t running anymore.\n\nSo, the next logical step is to list all the pods associated with the ad service. Using `kubectl get pods -l app=ad -n astronomy-shop` will show the current pods. Once they have the correct pod name, they can then retrieve the logs to check for any errors or misconfigurations that might be causing the redirects. This approach ensures they get the most up-to-date information and avoid the "not found" error.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get pods -l app=ad -n astronomy-shop"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-a1cc617d1f634741', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 247, 'prompt_tokens': 13055, 'total_tokens': 13302, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfed2-fcba-7281-bc33-daba78c92cfa-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get pods -l app=ad -n astronomy-shop'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-a1cc617d1f634741', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 13055, 'output_tokens': 247, 'total_tokens': 13302}), ToolMessage(content='', id='eb01475b-2b86-4148-a844-8ee02da22d25', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-a1cc617d1f634741'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='4df7df98-58f9-40f8-9a87-d1699d0aed21'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is trying to diagnose an issue with the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application. The problem seems to be related to the frontend service causing 308 Permanent Redirects when calling the ad service. \n\nFirst, they checked the pods and services, confirming that the ad service exists and has endpoints. But when they tried to get logs for a specific pod, it wasn't found. Then they checked the pods labeled with app=ad, but the output was empty. That means there are no pods with that label currently running.\n\nWait, the dependency graph showed that the frontend is calling the ad service, and the traces have 308 redirects. The ad service's endpoints were listed, but the pod isn't found. Maybe the pod was recently deleted or the label is incorrect. The user tried to get the pod name using the label, but no pods were found. \n\nSo, the next step is to check if the ad service is actually running. Since the endpoints show an IP, but no pods are listed, maybe the pods are not properly labeled or there's a typo in the label selector. Alternatively, the service might be misconfigured to point to a non-existent pod. \n\nThe user should verify the deployment for the ad service. Checking the deployment configuration would show if the pods are being created with the correct labels. If the deployment is not running, that's a problem. Also, checking the service's YAML to ensure it's pointing to the right pods. \n\nBut since the user can only use the provided tools, the next logical step is to check the deployment of the ad service. Using `kubectl get deployment ad -n astronomy-shop` would show if the deployment exists and its status. If the deployment is not healthy, that could explain why the pods aren't showing up. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the ad service is using a different label or the deployment name is different. The user might need to check the deployment name and its associated pods. If the deployment is not running, that's the root cause. \n\nSo, the next tool call should be to get the deployment details for the ad service to see if it's properly configured and running. That would help determine if the issue is with the deployment not creating pods or the service misconfigured.\n</think>\n\nget_services  \nThe previous attempt to retrieve logs for the **ad** pod failed, and no pods were found with the label `app=ad`. This suggests either the service is misconfigured, the deployment is not running, or the label selector is incorrect. To verify if the **ad** service is properly deployed and associated with running pods, I will use `get_services` to check if the service is correctly linked to its deployment and pods in the `astronomy-shop` namespace. This will confirm if the service is functional or misconfigured.", additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 579, 'prompt_tokens': 12244, 'total_tokens': 12823, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfed3-0c1d-7f60-9051-e20f9c738975-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 12244, 'output_tokens': 579, 'total_tokens': 12823}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='29534fe5-aa51-4f78-b496-bcd696d91928'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to diagnose an issue with the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application. The problem seems to be related to the frontend service causing 308 Permanent Redirects when calling the ad service. \n\nFirst, they checked the pods and services, found that the ad service exists as a ClusterIP with endpoints, but when trying to get logs for the ad pod, it wasn\'t found. Then they tried to list pods with the label app=ad, but there were no pods found. That\'s confusing because the service exists but no pods are running with that label.\n\nThe user then decided to use the get_services tool to check if the ad service is properly linked to its deployment and pods. The get_services tool retrieves service names from Grafana, but earlier when they used get_services, it returned nothing. Wait, maybe the services tool isn\'t the right one here. The user might need to check the Kubernetes services directly instead of relying on Grafana. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the ad service is not properly configured, and the deployment for ad isn\'t running. Since the pod with the label app=ad isn\'t found, perhaps the deployment is misconfigured or the pods are not being created. The user should check the deployment status or the service\'s YAML to see if the selector is correct. But given the tools available, the next step would be to verify the service\'s configuration to ensure it\'s pointing to the correct pods. \n\nWait, the user is using the get_services tool, which might not be the right approach here. The get_services tool is supposed to get service names from Grafana, but if the Grafana instance doesn\'t have the services listed, that\'s a problem. However, the user already checked the Kubernetes services via kubectl and found the ad service exists. The issue is that the pods aren\'t running with the expected label. \n\nSo, maybe the correct approach is to check the deployment for the ad service. The user could use kubectl to get the deployment and check its status. But the available tools don\'t include a direct way to get deployments. The exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd tool can be used to run commands like kubectl get deployments. \n\nWait, the user has the exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd tool, which allows running kubectl commands. So instead of using get_services, they should use exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd to check the deployment for the ad service. For example, run "kubectl get deployments -n astronomy-shop" to see if the ad deployment exists and is in a healthy state. \n\nBut the user\'s last step was to call get_services, which might not be the right tool. The get_services tool returns service names from Grafana, but the user needs to check the actual Kubernetes services and deployments. So the correct tool here would be exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd with the command "kubectl get deployments -n astronomy-shop" to check the deployment status of the ad service. \n\nAlternatively, if the deployment is correct, the user should check the pods again, maybe using a different label or checking the service\'s YAML to see if the selector is matching the pod\'s labels. But given the tools available, the next logical step is to check the deployment status using kubectl, which is possible with the exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd tool.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get deployments -n astronomy-shop"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b7722b30a875cbe4', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 709, 'prompt_tokens': 13259, 'total_tokens': 13968, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfed3-293b-75c0-bd7f-5275102dc3c7-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get deployments -n astronomy-shop'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b7722b30a875cbe4', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 13259, 'output_tokens': 709, 'total_tokens': 13968}), ToolMessage(content='NAME              READY   UP-TO-DATE   AVAILABLE   AGE\naccounting        1/1     1            1           5m57s\nad                1/1     1            1           5m57s\ncart              1/1     1            1           5m57s\ncheckout          1/1     1            1           5m57s\ncurrency          1/1     1            1           5m57s\nemail             1/1     1            1           5m57s\nflagd             1/1     1            1           5m57s\nfraud-detection   1/1     1            1           5m57s\nfrontend          1/1     1            1           5m57s\nfrontend-proxy    1/1     1            1           5m57s\ngrafana           1/1     1            1           5m57s\nimage-provider    1/1     1            1           5m57s\njaeger            1/1     1            1           5m57s\nkafka             1/1     1            1           5m57s\nllm               1/1     1            1           5m57s\nload-generator    1/1     1            1           5m57s\npayment           1/1     1            1           5m57s\npostgresql        1/1     1            1           5m57s\nproduct-catalog   1/1     1            1           5m57s\nproduct-reviews   1/1     1            1           5m57s\nquote             1/1     1            1           5m57s\nrecommendation    1/1     1            1           5m57s\nshipping          1/1     1            1           5m57s\nvalkey-cart       1/1     1            1           5m57s\n', id='42d2d6e8-938c-4af7-bc00-b9b2b341289c', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-b7722b30a875cbe4'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='37d06c1c-34a6-4cab-8e78-b5e433531d7f')]]
