why they're returning 308 redirects, maybe a misconfiguration in the service's routing rules.\n</think>\n\nexec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nThe `ad` service exists as a ClusterIP but its reachability and pod health need verification. I will check the service's endpoints and pod status using `kubectl get endpoints ad -n astronomy-shop` and `kubectl get pods -l app=ad -n astronomy-shop` to ensure the service is properly routing traffic to healthy pods. This will confirm if the 308 redirects stem from service misconfiguration or pod unavailability.", additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 493, 'prompt_tokens': 11584, 'total_tokens': 12077, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfed2-78b1-7f73-8164-248b56b132ae-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 11584, 'output_tokens': 493, 'total_tokens': 12077}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='fe3468f3-0b7a-44ac-aff5-87aa55037ec1'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is trying to diagnose an issue with the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application. They've already checked the pods and found them all running. Then they looked at metrics and traces, which showed some 308 Permanent Redirects from the frontend to the ad service. The dependency graph shows frontend calling ad, and the operations list includes calls to AdService/GetAds.\n\nThe next step was to check the ad service's Kubernetes service and endpoints. The service exists as a ClusterIP, but they need to ensure that the endpoints are correctly set up and that the pods are healthy. So, the user should run `kubectl get endpoints ad -n astronomy-shop` to check if there are any endpoints associated with the service. If there are no endpoints, that means the service isn't properly routing to the pods. Also, they should check the pods labeled with app=ad to make sure they're running and ready. If the pods are not in a Ready state or if there are no pods matching the label, that could explain the redirects. So, the next tool call should be to get the endpoints and pods for the ad service.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get endpoints ad -n astronomy-shop"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-8e413040451618c8', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 271, 'prompt_tokens': 12584, 'total_tokens': 12855, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfed2-9159-7d52-a2e9-432934ec60cc-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get endpoints ad -n astronomy-shop'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-8e413040451618c8', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 12584, 'output_tokens': 271, 'total_tokens': 12855}), ToolMessage(content='NAME   ENDPOINTS           AGE\nad     10.244.0.244:8080   5m13s\n', id='74509efd-b292-4f69-8b67-5908e9999167', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-8e413040451618c8'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='ae9b3251-d840-497e-9f2c-bc14d1061450'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is trying to diagnose an issue with the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application. So far, they've checked the services, pods, metrics, traces, dependency graph, and operations.