 If not, investigate why the deployment isn\'t creating pods with the correct labels. This should help identify whether the issue is with the service configuration, pod labels, or something else causing the 308 redirects.\n</think>\n\nexec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nThe `ad` deployment uses the label `opentelemetry.io/name=ad` in its selector, but earlier attempts to find pods failed when using `app=ad`. To resolve this, I will directly query pods labeled with `opentelemetry.io/name=ad` to identify the correct pod name. This ensures alignment with the deployment\'s selector and avoids mismatches due to stale or incorrect labels. \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd", "arguments": {"command": "kubectl get pods -n astronomy-shop -l opentelemetry.io/name=ad"}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=605, prompt_tokens=14048, total_tokens=14653, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfed3-7a43-7880-8fb5-fe40a0d9bf14-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 14048, 'output_tokens': 605, 'total_tokens': 14653}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='d28d8dd9-a8d9-4c96-a4db-b24e00fd63e5')]]
