ent. Alternatively, use "kubectl get pods -l app=ad -n astronomy-shop" to list all pods with the app label set to ad. That might give the correct pod name. So, the user should run "kubectl get deployments -n astronomy-shop" to find the deployment for the ad service, then get the pods from that deployment. Alternatively, use the label selector. Let me proceed with that.\n</think>\n\nexec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nThe pod "ad-6c7d4665cc-h454d" was not found, suggesting it may have been deleted or renamed. To accurately retrieve logs, I will first identify the current pod name associated with the **ad** service using `kubectl get pods -l app=ad -n astronomy-shop`. This ensures I target the correct running pod, avoiding errors from stale or incorrect pod names.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 959, 'prompt_tokens': 12057, 'total_tokens': 13016, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfed2-ccaf-7923-b5e3-dcf2f1be18c3-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 12057, 'output_tokens': 959, 'total_tokens': 13016}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='ac7c87ef-c220-476c-8883-c3b533e48b9e'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to diagnose an issue with the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application. The problem seems to be related to the frontend service causing 308 Permanent Redirects when calling the ad service. \n\nFirst, they checked the pods and services, confirming that the ad service exists and has endpoints. But when they tried to get the logs of a specific pod (ad-6c7d4665cc-h454d), it wasn\'t found. That means the pod name might have changed or the pod isn\'t running anymore.\n\nSo, the next logical step is to list all the pods associated with the ad service. Using `kubectl get pods -l app=ad -n astronomy-shop` will show the current pods. Once they have the correct pod name, they can then retrieve the logs to check for any errors or misconfigurations that might be causing the redirects. This approach ensures they get the most up-to-date information and avoid the "not found" error.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get pods -l app=ad -n astronomy-shop"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-a1cc617d1f634741', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 247, 'prompt_tokens': 13055, 'total_tokens': 13302, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfed2-fcba-7281-bc33-daba78c92cfa-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get pods -l app=ad -n astronomy-shop'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-a1cc617d1f634741', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 13055, 'output_tokens': 247, 'total_tokens': 13302}), ToolMessage(content='', id='eb01475b-2b86-4148-a844-8ee02da22d25', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-a1cc617d1f634741'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='4df7df98-58f9-40f8-9a87-d1699d0aed21'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is trying to diagnose an issue with the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application. The problem seems to be related to the frontend service causing 308 Permanent Redirects when calling the ad service. \n\nFirst, they checked